╭─ Issue description ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Issue Title: [BUG] Bedrock Mantle base-path table only handles openai.gpt-5.*, mis-routing xai.grok-4.3 (and every third-party model) to /v1    │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Description:                                                                                                                                    │
│ ### Checks                                                                                                                                      │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ -  I have updated to the lastest minor and patch version of Strands                                                                             │
│ -  I have checked the documentation and this is not expected behavior                                                                           │
│ -  I have searched ./issues and there are no duplicates of my issue                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### SDK Language                                                                                                                                │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ TypeScript                                                                                                                                      │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Strands Version                                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Reported against current `main` / latest published `@strands-agents/sdk`. Exact version not captured from the reporter — the routing defect     │
│ below is present on `main` as of this filing.                                                                                                   │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Language Runtime Version                                                                                                                    │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Not captured from the reporter (Node.js).                                                                                                       │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Operating System                                                                                                                            │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Not captured from the reporter.                                                                                                                 │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Installation Method                                                                                                                         │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ npm                                                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Steps to Reproduce                                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Reported by a user attempting to reach `xai.grok-4.3` through the Bedrock Mantle endpoint in `us-east-1`                                        │
│ (`https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-1.api.aws`).                                                                                                   │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ```ts                                                                                                                                           │
│ import { OpenAIModel } from '@strands-agents/sdk/models/openai'                                                                                 │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ const model = new OpenAIModel({                                                                                                                 │
│   modelId: 'xai.grok-4.3',                                                                                                                      │
│   bedrockMantleConfig: { region: 'us-east-1' },                                                                                                 │
│ })                                                                                                                                              │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ await model.stream([{ role: 'user', content: [{ text: 'hello' }] }])                                                                            │
│ ```                                                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ The model id is valid and servable-by-catalog: `GET /v1/models` on the same endpoint returns `xai.grok-4.3` with `"status":"available"`, so     │
│ this is not a typo'd or unavailable model id.                                                                                                   │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ The reporter also exercised the three routes directly with `curl` to isolate the SDK from the service:                                          │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ | Route | Payload shape | HTTP | Response |                                                                                                     │
│ |---|---|---|---|                                                                                                                               │
│ | `/v1/chat/completions` | Chat Completions | 400 | `{"error":{"code":"validation_error","message":"model 'xai.grok-4.3' isn't supported on     │
│ this route","type":"invalid_request_error"}}` |                                                                                                 │
│ | `/openai/v1/chat/completions` | Chat Completions | 500 | `{"error":{"code":"internal_server_error","message":"The server had an error while   │
│ processing your request. Sorry about that!","type":"server_error"}}` |                                                                          │
│ | `/openai/v1/responses` | Responses API | 500 | same `internal_server_error` body |                                                            │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Control case, same account, same credentials, same session: `google.gemma-4-31b` returns valid completions on **`/openai/v1/chat/completions`** │
│ and **`/openai/v1/responses`**. That rules out credentials, account permissions, and client code.                                               │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Expected Behavior                                                                                                                           │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Two separate expectations, because there are two separate defects here — one ours, one not.                                                     │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ 1. `OpenAIModel` + `bedrockMantleConfig` should route a non-OpenAI-family Mantle model id (`xai.*`, `google.*`, `anthropic.*`) to the base path │
│ Mantle actually serves it from. It should not construct a request against a route the service will reject with `validation_error`.              │
│ 2. A model advertised as `"status":"available"` by `GET /v1/models` should be invocable on at least one route.                                  │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Actual Behavior                                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ **Defect 1 (SDK, actionable here): the Mantle base-path table only special-cases `openai.gpt-5.*`, so every third-party model id falls through  │
│ to `/v1` — the route that 400s.**                                                                                                               │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ `strands-ts/src/models/openai/mantle.ts`:                                                                                                       │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ```ts                                                                                                                                           │
│ const OPENAI_PATH_MODEL_PREFIXES = ['openai.gpt-5.'] as const                                                                                   │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ export function bedrockMantleBaseUrl(region: string, modelId: string): string {                                                                 │
│   const suffix = OPENAI_PATH_MODEL_PREFIXES.some((prefix) => modelId.startsWith(prefix)) ? '/openai/v1' : '/v1'                                 │
│   return `https://bedrock-mantle.${region}.api.aws${suffix}`                                                                                    │
│ }                                                                                                                                               │
│ ```                                                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ `xai.grok-4.3` does not start with `openai.gpt-5.`, so it resolves to `/v1` — and `/v1/chat/completions` is precisely the route that returns    │
│ `model 'xai.grok-4.3' isn't supported on this route`. The SDK cannot currently be pointed at `/openai/v1` for this model either, since          │
│ `bedrockMantleConfig` rejects a caller-supplied `clientConfig.baseURL` (validated in `mantle.test.ts`, "throws when `clientConfig.baseURL` is   │
│ set alongside `bedrockMantleConfig`"). There is no supported escape hatch.                                                                      │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ The reporter's own control case is the proof that the table is wrong, not just incomplete: `google.gemma-4-31b` **works** on `/openai/v1`, but  │
│ the SDK would route it to `/v1` for the same reason. So the mis-routing is not specific to Grok — it applies to every non-`openai.gpt-5.*` id,  │
│ and it is currently masked only because those models aren't documented as supported yet (#3563).                                                │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ The comment in `mantle.ts` states the operative rule correctly ("the base path is keyed by model family, not API surface") but the prefix list  │
│ encodes only the OpenAI families that existed when it was written.                                                                              │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ **Defect 2 (Mantle service-side, not fixable in this repo): `/openai/v1/*` 500s for `xai.grok-4.3`.**                                           │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Once routed to `/openai/v1`, Grok returns `internal_server_error` on both Chat Completions and Responses, while Gemma succeeds on the same      │
│ routes with the same credentials. That is a serving-side problem with this specific model, either a catalog mis-registration (advertised        │
│ `available`, not actually servable) or a backend fault. Fixing Defect 1 will **not** make `xai.grok-4.3` work; it will change a 400 into a 500  │
│ until the service side is resolved. Worth cutting a separate ticket to the Bedrock Mantle service team, and worth confirming Grok is servable   │
│ before wiring it up here — otherwise SDK-side support cannot be integ-tested.                                                                   │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Additional Context                                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Parity: the Python SDK has the identical defect at `strands-py/src/strands/models/_openai_bedrock.py`:                                          │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ```python                                                                                                                                       │
│ _OPENAI_PATH_MODEL_PREFIXES: tuple = ("openai.gpt-5.",)                                                                                         │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ def _resolve_mantle_base_path(model_id: str) -> str:                                                                                            │
│     if model_id.startswith(_OPENAI_PATH_MODEL_PREFIXES):                                                                                        │
│         return "/openai/v1"                                                                                                                     │
│     return "/v1"                                                                                                                                │
│ ```                                                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Any fix should land in both SDKs to preserve parity.                                                                                            │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Related history on this same base-path logic, all of which suggests the prefix-matching approach is fragile enough to be worth replacing rather │
│ than extending:                                                                                                                                 │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ - #3279 — `[BUG] OpenAIModel Bedrock Mantle base URL is wrong for the Responses API (hits /v1/responses)` (closed)                              │
│ - #2629 — `bedrock_mantle_config builds wrong base_url for OpenAI Responses models (missing /openai path segment)` (closed)                     │
│ - #3388 — `OpenAIModel (Responses, TypeScript) sends invalid assistant history shape, rejected by Bedrock Mantle` (closed)                      │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ This is the fourth bug filed against Mantle base-URL/route derivation.                                                                          │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Possible Solution                                                                                                                           │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Scoped to Defect 1 only.                                                                                                                        │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ The narrow fix is to add the third-party families to the prefix list so they resolve to `/openai/v1`:                                           │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ```ts                                                                                                                                           │
│ const OPENAI_PATH_MODEL_PREFIXES = ['openai.gpt-5.', 'xai.', 'google.', 'anthropic.'] as const                                                  │
│ ```                                                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ That is a one-line change, mirrored in Python, and it makes the confirmed-working case (`google.gemma-4-31b` on `/openai/v1`) actually          │
│ reachable through the SDK. But it keeps the design that has now produced four bugs: a hardcoded allowlist of prefixes that must be updated      │
│ every time Mantle onboards a family, where the failure mode is a confusing service-side 400 rather than a clear client-side error.              │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Two alternatives worth weighing during triage:                                                                                                  │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ 1. **Invert the default.** `/openai/v1` appears to be the general case and `/v1` the exception (`openai.gpt-oss-*`). Encoding the exceptions    │
│ instead of the rule shrinks the list that needs maintenance and makes new families work by default.                                             │
│ 2. **Fail loudly on unrecognized families.** If the model id matches no known Mantle family, throw a client-side error naming the id and the    │
│ supported prefixes rather than silently building a URL that the service will reject. That converts an opaque `validation_error` from Mantle     │
│ into an actionable message, which is what the reporter needed here.                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Either way, extending the allowlist without also deciding on the default is likely to produce bug number five.                                  │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Also worth considering: whether `bedrockMantleConfig`'s hard rejection of `clientConfig.baseURL` should relax to a documented override. The     │
│ validation is sound as a default (it prevents accidentally unsigned or mis-pointed requests), but with no escape hatch, a routing-table gap is  │
│ a hard block rather than a workaround-able annoyance.                                                                                           │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Related Issues                                                                                                                              │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ #3563 (feature request: Mantle-API support for Anthropic, Google and Grok models). This issue is the bug half of that request: the routing      │
│ table silently mis-routes those families today rather than rejecting them, so the failure surfaces as an opaque service 400.                    │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
